# Mysterium Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (local dev) or set as Cloudflare secrets (prod).
# All variables are OPTIONAL — the game runs in degraded mode without them.

# ─── LLM Provider (BFF /api/llm/*) ─────────────────────────────────
# The BFF reads the API key server-side. The browser NEVER sees it.
# Set ONE of the following:

# Option A: Generic LLM config (recommended — provider-agnostic)
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai|anthropic
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Option B: Provider-specific shortcuts
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ─── Cloudflare Bindings (wrangler.toml declares these) ────────────
# These are NOT set as env vars — they're declared in wrangler.toml
# and injected as platform.env in +server.ts endpoints:
#   - SAVE_KV: Workers KV namespace for encrypted save blobs
#   - RECOVERY_KV: Workers KV namespace for mnemonic → deviceId mapping
#   - ANALYTICS: Analytics Engine for telemetry event ingestion

# ─── Client-side (exposed to browser — safe) ───────────────────────
# Public config uses VITE_ prefix so Vite exposes it to the client.
# These are safe to expose — no secrets here.

# The BFF base URL. Defaults to '' (same-origin). Set this if the BFF
# runs on a different domain than the game shell.
# VITE_BFF_BASE_URL=https://api.mysterium.game

# ─── Dev-only flags ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 1 to enable verbose VeilFilter logging in the console.
# Mysterium_DEV=1
